Chapter: E1000LinkBudget
  cites Kernel chapter E1000e
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `e1000-await-link` was bounded by a count of four million and nothing else. It
 never showed while `e1000-await-aneg` was burning 92.9 seconds ahead of it,
 because the link came up during that dead time and this loop was answered on
 its first pass. Budgeting aneg exposed it: measured on the ASUS 2026-08-16,
 over ten minutes with no return. It is bounded by a duration now.

 WHAT THIS ARM COVERS, and what covers the rest. This one is arithmetic only:
 the budget derivation and the poll coverage, which are the halves most likely
 to be silently wrong and which need no device. The TIMEOUT BEHAVIOUR is not
 here and does not need to be, because `-e1000-no-link` reaches it and
 `codex/test/e1000-link-deadline` is that arm.

 An earlier draft of this paragraph said the timeout branch was unreachable in
 the bed, by analogy with `e1000-aneg-budget` where it genuinely is. That was
 wrong and the flag had existed for some time: `e1000-asde-nolink` was already
 running under it. The analogy was the whole of the reasoning and no one checked
 it, which is the failure this project keeps writing down -- an instrument
 pointed at part of the question and read as an answer to all of it.

 THE PROPERTY IS THE SAME WALL TIME AT DIFFERENT RATES, which is the whole
 point of a budget: a count gives different durations on different machines.
 Both real HPET rates this project has measured are here, the ASUS 23999999 and
 the bed 14318179, and both must yield five seconds.

 THE SECOND PROPERTY IS THAT NOTHING GOT LESS SENSITIVE. Moving from a bare
 count to a clocked batch must not reduce how many times the link can be polled
 before giving up, or a slow link that used to be caught would start being
 missed. batch * batch-fuel is the new ceiling and it must not fall below the
 old four million.

 We say:

Section: Fixtures

  metal-hz : Integer = 23999999
  bed-hz : Integer = 14318179

  seconds-of : Integer -> Integer
  seconds-of (rate) = if rate <= 0 then (0 - 1) else (e1000-link-ticks rate) / rate

  max-polls : Integer = e1000-link-batch * e1000-link-batch-fuel

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("window-ms=" & show e1000-link-window-ms)
    print-line-uni ("metal-ticks=" & show (e1000-link-ticks metal-hz))
    print-line-uni ("metal-seconds=" & show (seconds-of metal-hz))
    print-line-uni ("bed-ticks=" & show (e1000-link-ticks bed-hz))
    print-line-uni ("bed-seconds=" & show (seconds-of bed-hz))
    print-line-uni ("same-wall-time=" & show (seconds-of metal-hz == seconds-of bed-hz))
    print-line-uni ("zero-rate-ticks=" & show (e1000-link-ticks 0))
    print-line-uni ("count-still-a-bound=" & show (e1000-link-fuel > 0))
    print-line-uni ("max-polls=" & show max-polls)
    print-line-uni ("no-less-sensitive=" & show (max-polls >= e1000-link-fuel))
  end
